1
00:00:02,628 --> 00:00:03,712
MONICA:
Hey, hon?

2
00:00:03,754 --> 00:00:05,923
Would you help me
get the plates down?

3
00:00:05,965 --> 00:00:07,591
Yeah. Hey,
here's an idea.

4
00:00:07,633 --> 00:00:09,301
Why don't we use
our wedding china today?

5
00:00:09,343 --> 00:00:10,803
No. I think we should
save our china

6
00:00:10,845 --> 00:00:12,137
for something really special.

7
00:00:12,179 --> 00:00:15,432
Like... if the Queen
of England comes over.

8
00:00:15,474 --> 00:00:17,392
Honey, she keeps canceling
on us.

9
00:00:17,434 --> 00:00:18,978
Take the hint.

10
00:00:19,019 --> 00:00:20,813
What... what if something
gets broken?

11
00:00:20,855 --> 00:00:22,690
They're so expensive.

12
00:00:22,731 --> 00:00:24,650
What is the point
of having them if
we never use them?

13
00:00:24,692 --> 00:00:26,652
Okay, but if something
gets broken

14
00:00:26,694 --> 00:00:28,570
and then the Queen
comes over...

15
00:00:28,612 --> 00:00:30,113
I will explain it to her.

16
00:00:30,155 --> 00:00:32,407
Oh, yeah. Like I'm going
to let you talk to the Queen.

17
00:00:34,159 --> 00:00:37,371
Wow, the parade is really good
this year.

18
00:00:37,412 --> 00:00:39,331
Man, those horses can crap.

19
00:00:39,373 --> 00:00:42,167
TV ANNOUNCER:
Next up is a marching band

20
00:00:42,209 --> 00:00:43,544
from Muskogee, Oklahoma.

21
00:00:43,585 --> 00:00:46,839
Muskogee? That's, like,
four hours from Tulsa!

22
00:00:46,881 --> 00:00:48,757
Whoo-hoo!

23
00:00:48,799 --> 00:00:50,175
ANNOUNCER:
And here comes the float

24
00:00:50,217 --> 00:00:51,927
with the stars
of the popular daytime soap

25
00:00:51,969 --> 00:00:53,971
Days of Our Lives.

26
00:00:57,140 --> 00:00:58,475
Oh, my God!

27
00:00:58,517 --> 00:01:00,185
Aren't you one
of the stars

28
00:01:00,227 --> 00:01:02,479
of the popular daytime
soap Days of Our Lives?

29
00:01:02,521 --> 00:01:03,814
Yeah!

30
00:01:03,856 --> 00:01:07,234
I totally forgot,
I'm supposed to be there.

31
00:01:07,275 --> 00:01:09,110
I can't believe I forgot.

32
00:01:09,152 --> 00:01:11,947
I usually write stuff
like this down on my arm.

33
00:01:13,448 --> 00:01:14,616
Oh!

34
00:01:14,658 --> 00:01:17,452
Stupid long sleeves!

35
00:01:17,494 --> 00:01:19,830
What are you going to do?

36
00:01:19,872 --> 00:01:21,331
I guess I'm going
to have to come up

37
00:01:21,373 --> 00:01:23,250
with a really good reason
why I wasn't there.

38
00:01:23,291 --> 00:01:25,084
The producers are going
to be so mad at me.

39
00:01:25,126 --> 00:01:26,587
They sat us all down yesterday

40
00:01:26,628 --> 00:01:28,923
and said, "Everyone has
to be there 6:00 a.m. sharp.

41
00:01:28,964 --> 00:01:30,925
That means you, Tribbiani."

42
00:01:30,966 --> 00:01:34,678
Like... like I was
some kind of idiot.

43
00:01:35,721 --> 00:01:37,556
Well, you proved
them wrong.

44
00:01:37,598 --> 00:01:38,724
Yeah.

45
00:01:45,188 --> 00:01:50,360
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

46
00:01:50,402 --> 00:01:52,696
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

47
00:01:52,738 --> 00:01:55,198
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

48
00:01:55,240 --> 00:02:00,079
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

49
00:02:00,119 --> 00:02:02,081
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

50
00:02:02,122 --> 00:02:04,666
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

51
00:02:04,708 --> 00:02:08,754
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

52
00:02:08,796 --> 00:02:09,922
♪ When the rain starts to pour ♪

53
00:02:09,964 --> 00:02:12,549
♪ I'll be there for you ♪

54
00:02:12,591 --> 00:02:14,927
♪ Like I've been there before ♪

55
00:02:14,969 --> 00:02:18,680
♪ I'll be there for you ♪

56
00:02:18,722 --> 00:02:22,517
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

57
00:02:28,774 --> 00:02:31,902
Oh, Emma.

58
00:02:31,944 --> 00:02:34,947
This is your first
Thanksgiving.

59
00:02:34,989 --> 00:02:37,532
What are you thankful for?

60
00:02:37,574 --> 00:02:39,534
Mommy's boobies?

61
00:02:39,576 --> 00:02:42,997
A lot of people are
thankful for those.

62
00:02:43,038 --> 00:02:45,248
( knocking on door )

63
00:02:45,290 --> 00:02:47,334
WOMAN:
Hello? Rachel?

64
00:02:47,375 --> 00:02:48,710
Who is it?

65
00:02:48,752 --> 00:02:51,379
It's your
favorite sister.

66
00:02:51,421 --> 00:02:52,673
Jill?
Jill?

67
00:02:52,714 --> 00:02:54,257
Amy.

68
00:02:54,299 --> 00:02:55,383
Hide my rings.

69
00:02:55,425 --> 00:02:57,469
( groans )

70
00:03:00,681 --> 00:03:01,974
Amy!

71
00:03:02,016 --> 00:03:04,018
Happy Thanksgiving.

72
00:03:08,772 --> 00:03:11,441
Do you have a hair straightener?

73
00:03:11,483 --> 00:03:13,610
Um... hi.

74
00:03:13,652 --> 00:03:14,945
Oh.

75
00:03:14,987 --> 00:03:16,195
Aw...
Hi...

76
00:03:16,237 --> 00:03:17,781
Hair straightener.

77
00:03:17,823 --> 00:03:18,949
( chuckles )

78
00:03:18,991 --> 00:03:20,909
I haven't see you
in, like, a year.

79
00:03:20,951 --> 00:03:22,077
Oh, I know, I know.

80
00:03:22,119 --> 00:03:23,370
I've just been crazed.

81
00:03:23,411 --> 00:03:24,955
Oh, well, yeah, me, too.

82
00:03:24,997 --> 00:03:26,790
Um, I had a baby.

83
00:03:26,832 --> 00:03:28,876
I decorated Dad's office.

84
00:03:28,917 --> 00:03:30,836
Oh, yeah?

85
00:03:30,878 --> 00:03:33,547
Well, unless you pushed
a desk out of your vagina

86
00:03:33,588 --> 00:03:36,008
not the same thing.

87
00:03:36,050 --> 00:03:38,385
Listen, um, about that
hair straightener, honey

88
00:03:38,426 --> 00:03:40,637
I really need one--
I'm going to have dinner

89
00:03:40,679 --> 00:03:43,015
at my boyfriend's house.

90
00:03:43,057 --> 00:03:45,350
Oh, my God.
Mm-hmm.

91
00:03:45,392 --> 00:03:47,144
Is this Emmet?

92
00:03:51,523 --> 00:03:54,109
Uh, it's Emma.

93
00:03:54,151 --> 00:03:55,777
It's a girl?

94
00:03:57,071 --> 00:03:58,238
Hey, Amy.

95
00:03:58,279 --> 00:04:00,281
Oh, Amy, you
remember Ross.

96
00:04:00,323 --> 00:04:03,243
Uh... not really.

97
00:04:03,284 --> 00:04:07,247
But... you are much cuter than
that geeky guy she used to date.

98
00:04:09,917 --> 00:04:13,087
That was me.
No.

99
00:04:13,128 --> 00:04:15,047
He was this creepy guy
from high school

100
00:04:15,089 --> 00:04:16,631
who had this huge crush on her

101
00:04:16,673 --> 00:04:18,217
since, like,
the ninth grade.

102
00:04:18,257 --> 00:04:20,260
Still me.

103
00:04:20,301 --> 00:04:21,803
No, I'm not talking about you.

104
00:04:21,845 --> 00:04:23,889
Come on, it was
your fat friend's brother

105
00:04:23,931 --> 00:04:25,724
with that bad afro,
do you remember?

106
00:04:25,766 --> 00:04:27,935
Okay, Amy, I'm going to save you
some time, okay?

107
00:04:27,976 --> 00:04:29,978
All me.

108
00:04:34,315 --> 00:04:35,901
Careful.

109
00:04:35,943 --> 00:04:37,986
Careful.

110
00:04:38,028 --> 00:04:40,321
Careful! Sorry.

111
00:04:40,363 --> 00:04:41,531
I'll tell you what.

112
00:04:41,573 --> 00:04:43,075
For the rest of our lives

113
00:04:43,117 --> 00:04:45,660
I'll be careful
until told otherwise.

114
00:04:45,702 --> 00:04:50,249
Wait a minute, this isn't
the china we picked out.
I know.

115
00:04:50,289 --> 00:04:52,667
After you left the store,
I chose different ones.

116
00:04:52,709 --> 00:04:55,420
Why?

117
00:04:55,462 --> 00:04:56,922
Well, no offense, honey

118
00:04:56,964 --> 00:04:58,506
but your taste is
a little feminine for me.

119
00:04:58,548 --> 00:05:01,218
Oh, suddenly flowers
are feminine?

120
00:05:01,260 --> 00:05:03,053
Hey, everybody!

121
00:05:03,095 --> 00:05:06,431
Happy Thanksgiving.
Hey, happy Thanksgiving.
Pheebs...

122
00:05:06,473 --> 00:05:07,849
Hey, what's going on, Joe?

123
00:05:07,891 --> 00:05:09,768
I-I-I need a good lie.

124
00:05:09,810 --> 00:05:11,770
Oh. Okay.

125
00:05:11,812 --> 00:05:16,024
How about the whole "man walking
on the Moon" thing, you know?

126
00:05:16,066 --> 00:05:20,112
You-you could... you could
see the strings, people.

127
00:05:20,154 --> 00:05:22,281
No, no, no. I need
a good lie to explain

128
00:05:22,322 --> 00:05:24,199
why I wasn't at a
work thing today.

129
00:05:24,241 --> 00:05:25,993
Ooh, honey,
you stink at lying.

130
00:05:26,034 --> 00:05:27,327
I do not.

131
00:05:27,368 --> 00:05:29,204
Oh, really? Okay,
let me ask you something.

132
00:05:29,246 --> 00:05:30,705
Yesterday at the coffee house

133
00:05:30,747 --> 00:05:32,874
I went to the bathroom,
and when I came back

134
00:05:32,916 --> 00:05:34,542
my muffin was gone--
who took it?

135
00:05:35,585 --> 00:05:37,879
Somebody opened the door
to the coffee house

136
00:05:37,921 --> 00:05:39,380
and a raccoon
came running in

137
00:05:39,422 --> 00:05:41,216
and went straight
for your muffin.

138
00:05:41,258 --> 00:05:43,551
I said, "Hey, don't eat
that-- that's Phoebe's."

139
00:05:43,593 --> 00:05:45,762
And he said...

140
00:05:47,430 --> 00:05:49,557
He said, "Joey,
you stink at lying."

141
00:05:49,599 --> 00:05:50,976
What am I going to do?

142
00:05:51,018 --> 00:05:52,560
Don't worry, don't worry.

143
00:05:52,602 --> 00:05:53,687
We'll come up
with a good lie.

144
00:05:53,728 --> 00:05:54,896
I'll help you practice it.

145
00:05:54,938 --> 00:05:56,315
Oh, great, that'd
be great. Thank you.

146
00:05:56,355 --> 00:05:58,441
Sure. What-what was
the work thing?

147
00:05:58,483 --> 00:06:00,152
Uh...

148
00:06:00,194 --> 00:06:01,945
"Pick up Grandma
at the airport"?

149
00:06:01,987 --> 00:06:03,446
Oh, man...

150
00:06:06,283 --> 00:06:08,994
Oh, she's precious.

151
00:06:09,036 --> 00:06:11,872
Do you ever worry that she's
going to get your real nose?

152
00:06:12,914 --> 00:06:15,167
Amy...

153
00:06:15,209 --> 00:06:16,835
Yes, I do.

154
00:06:16,877 --> 00:06:17,961
I really do.

155
00:06:18,003 --> 00:06:19,378
( cell phone rings )

156
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:24,383
Hello?

157
00:06:24,425 --> 00:06:26,761
Yeah. Um, hang on one sec.

158
00:06:26,803 --> 00:06:29,181
Can I take this upstairs?
Sure.

159
00:06:29,223 --> 00:06:30,974
We don't live there, but...

160
00:06:31,016 --> 00:06:32,934
AMY:
Seriously?

161
00:06:32,976 --> 00:06:36,188
It's-it's just these rooms?

162
00:06:36,230 --> 00:06:38,940
I thought you were a doctor.

163
00:06:38,982 --> 00:06:40,483
Yeah, no, Ross has a PhD.

164
00:06:40,525 --> 00:06:42,527
Ew.

165
00:06:46,073 --> 00:06:49,617
God, she is unbelievable.

166
00:06:49,659 --> 00:06:52,913
I know. I mean,
a PhD is just as good as an MD.

167
00:06:52,954 --> 00:06:54,539
Oh, sure, Ross, yeah.

168
00:06:54,581 --> 00:06:56,833
If I have a heart attack
in a restaurant

169
00:06:56,875 --> 00:06:59,460
I want you there
with your fossil brush.

170
00:07:00,879 --> 00:07:02,797
Stupid Thanksgiving.

171
00:07:02,839 --> 00:07:04,841
What? What?
What happened?

172
00:07:04,883 --> 00:07:06,593
My boyfriend canceled on me.

173
00:07:06,634 --> 00:07:09,096
I mean, I... I finally find
a real relationship

174
00:07:09,137 --> 00:07:11,431
I mean, someone that I
can spend this day with

175
00:07:11,472 --> 00:07:14,393
and then his wife
comes back into town.

176
00:07:14,433 --> 00:07:18,063
I swear, it's almost
not even worth dating
married guys.

177
00:07:18,105 --> 00:07:20,274
Don't say that.

178
00:07:20,315 --> 00:07:23,985
Oh, I was so looking forward
to this.

179
00:07:24,027 --> 00:07:27,030
It was going to be
such a beautiful Thanksgiving.

180
00:07:27,072 --> 00:07:29,950
( sobbing ):
We were going to have sushi.

181
00:07:29,991 --> 00:07:33,828
Oh, Amy, don't cry.

182
00:07:33,870 --> 00:07:36,748
Um... Ross, could I talk
to you in private?

183
00:07:36,790 --> 00:07:38,708
Sure. You want
to go upstairs?

184
00:07:40,919 --> 00:07:43,255
Um...

185
00:07:43,297 --> 00:07:46,383
look, I was thinking,
if it's okay with Monica

186
00:07:46,425 --> 00:07:49,344
I would like to invite Amy
to Thanksgiving.

187
00:07:49,386 --> 00:07:51,471
You know, I think
that's a great idea.

188
00:07:51,512 --> 00:07:55,600
It'll be like the
pilgrims bringing
the Indians syphilis.

189
00:07:55,642 --> 00:07:58,186
Look, I know she's
a little tough to take...

190
00:07:58,228 --> 00:07:59,520
( groans )

191
00:07:59,562 --> 00:08:01,189
but she has nowhere else to go

192
00:08:01,231 --> 00:08:02,983
and she's my sister, all right?

193
00:08:03,024 --> 00:08:04,234
And she's Emma's aunt.

194
00:08:04,276 --> 00:08:06,361
And I would like them to bond.

195
00:08:06,403 --> 00:08:09,239
Okay, fine, but
I don't want them
bonding too much.

196
00:08:09,281 --> 00:08:12,200
I don't want her telling
Emma she needs a nose job.

197
00:08:12,242 --> 00:08:13,910
Ross, you know what?
She may need one.

198
00:08:13,952 --> 00:08:16,371
We're just going to have
to make our peace with that!

199
00:08:16,413 --> 00:08:18,581
( sighs )

200
00:08:23,295 --> 00:08:24,379
Hi.

201
00:08:24,421 --> 00:08:25,546
Hi.
Hey.

202
00:08:25,588 --> 00:08:26,881
Hey, you guys.

203
00:08:26,923 --> 00:08:28,549
This is my sister Amy.

204
00:08:28,591 --> 00:08:31,552
This is Chandler, Joey, Phoebe,
and you know Mon.

205
00:08:31,594 --> 00:08:33,221
Hi.
Hi.

206
00:08:33,263 --> 00:08:34,555
Oh, my God.

207
00:08:34,597 --> 00:08:36,599
You're on Days of Our Lives.

208
00:08:36,641 --> 00:08:38,726
( chuckles ):
Yeah.

209
00:08:38,768 --> 00:08:39,936
Wow.

210
00:08:39,978 --> 00:08:42,439
They must put
a lot of makeup on you.

211
00:08:44,107 --> 00:08:46,609
Hap-Hap-Happy Thanksgiving.

212
00:08:47,777 --> 00:08:49,863
Hey.
Hi.

213
00:08:49,904 --> 00:08:51,739
Hi, you.

214
00:08:51,781 --> 00:08:53,283
So, welcome.

215
00:08:53,325 --> 00:08:55,202
Is this the first time
you're seeing Emma?

216
00:08:55,243 --> 00:08:56,744
Yeah, I-I think so.

217
00:08:56,786 --> 00:08:58,497
It's nice to meet you, Emma.

218
00:09:00,581 --> 00:09:02,083
Phoebe.

219
00:09:02,125 --> 00:09:04,085
Oh. That's a funny noise.

220
00:09:08,215 --> 00:09:09,799
I still need
some help here.

221
00:09:09,841 --> 00:09:11,343
Oh, right. Okay, um...

222
00:09:11,385 --> 00:09:13,970
Okay, so it's not just
the lie you tell

223
00:09:14,012 --> 00:09:15,805
but it's the way you tell it.

224
00:09:15,847 --> 00:09:18,350
For example, if you
look down at the ground
when you're talking

225
00:09:18,392 --> 00:09:19,684
people know you're lying.

226
00:09:19,726 --> 00:09:21,853
Oh. I don't why this
is so hard for me.

227
00:09:21,895 --> 00:09:24,605
You know, I mean, lying
is basically just acting

228
00:09:24,647 --> 00:09:26,358
and I am a terrific actor.

229
00:09:26,400 --> 00:09:28,193
You are a terrific actor.

230
00:09:29,610 --> 00:09:31,654
Hey.

231
00:09:31,696 --> 00:09:33,031
Where's the baby?

232
00:09:33,073 --> 00:09:35,033
Oh, we just put her
down for her nap.

233
00:09:35,075 --> 00:09:36,701
Listen,
I was just thinking.

234
00:09:36,743 --> 00:09:38,786
You know what
would be incredible?

235
00:09:38,828 --> 00:09:41,748
If you guys died.

236
00:09:41,789 --> 00:09:45,210
Thank you, Amy.

237
00:09:45,252 --> 00:09:47,212
No, no,
then I would get the baby.

238
00:09:47,254 --> 00:09:49,548
I mean, you know,
it would be just like a movie.

239
00:09:49,589 --> 00:09:52,050
Like, at first, I wouldn't know
what to do with her

240
00:09:52,092 --> 00:09:53,885
and then I would rise
to the occasion

241
00:09:53,927 --> 00:09:55,636
and then-then I'd get a makeover

242
00:09:55,678 --> 00:09:57,055
and then I'd get married.

243
00:09:57,097 --> 00:09:59,640
That's a great movie!

244
00:09:59,682 --> 00:10:04,229
Now, listen, not that you guys
could stop me or anything

245
00:10:04,271 --> 00:10:06,898
'cause, you know,
you'd be dead, but...

246
00:10:06,940 --> 00:10:09,317
I was thinking about
changing her name.

247
00:10:09,359 --> 00:10:11,861
I'm just not really
a big fan of Emily.

248
00:10:11,903 --> 00:10:14,281
Emma.

249
00:10:15,656 --> 00:10:17,825
Emma, Ross wants you.

250
00:10:19,619 --> 00:10:21,121
Phoebe!

251
00:10:22,997 --> 00:10:26,543
Why does she keep making
that noise?

252
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:30,838
Honey, I don't know
how to tell you this

253
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:35,927
but, um, if something
were to happen to
Ross or myself...

254
00:10:35,969 --> 00:10:37,929
um, you wouldn't
get the baby.

255
00:10:37,971 --> 00:10:39,431
Well, who would?

256
00:10:39,473 --> 00:10:43,059
Well, we haven't officially
asked them yet

257
00:10:43,101 --> 00:10:45,812
but we would want
Monica and Chandler.

258
00:10:45,853 --> 00:10:48,898
I can't believe you'd
want us to raise Emma.

259
00:10:48,940 --> 00:10:51,067
Yeah, oh, my God,
I'm so moved.

260
00:10:51,109 --> 00:10:53,528
I don't believe this.
Hold on a second.

261
00:10:53,570 --> 00:10:56,615
You guys die,
and I don't get your baby?

262
00:10:56,656 --> 00:11:00,076
Look, Amy, see,
we're a lot closer to
Monica and Chandler.

263
00:11:00,118 --> 00:11:02,370
We see them every day,
and truthfully, honey

264
00:11:02,412 --> 00:11:04,623
you don't seem very
connected to the baby.

265
00:11:04,664 --> 00:11:06,583
Connected? I mean... to what?

266
00:11:06,625 --> 00:11:08,460
She's a lump.

267
00:11:10,629 --> 00:11:12,297
You know, guys,
I got to say

268
00:11:12,339 --> 00:11:13,881
this means
so much to me.

269
00:11:13,923 --> 00:11:17,135
I mean, that you would
trust me with your child.

270
00:11:17,177 --> 00:11:19,346
I mean, we all know
that Monica and I

271
00:11:19,387 --> 00:11:22,974
have been trying to have
a baby of our own, and...

272
00:11:23,016 --> 00:11:24,809
you know, I've
had my doubts

273
00:11:24,851 --> 00:11:28,480
about my skills
as a father, but...

274
00:11:28,522 --> 00:11:33,193
that you two...
that you two...

275
00:11:33,234 --> 00:11:36,070
This guy?

276
00:11:36,112 --> 00:11:38,156
Seriously?

277
00:11:43,411 --> 00:11:46,414
Okay!
It's time for dinner.

278
00:11:46,456 --> 00:11:49,292
Everyone, we're using
our fancy china

279
00:11:49,334 --> 00:11:52,795
and it's very expensive,
so please be careful.

280
00:11:54,130 --> 00:11:55,423
Whoa.

281
00:11:55,465 --> 00:11:56,883
Whoa...

282
00:11:56,924 --> 00:11:58,134
Whoa.

283
00:11:59,386 --> 00:12:00,761
Okay, just to be clear--

284
00:12:00,803 --> 00:12:03,348
comedy with the plates
will not be well received.

285
00:12:10,938 --> 00:12:12,232
Hey.

286
00:12:12,273 --> 00:12:13,525
How come my plate's

287
00:12:13,567 --> 00:12:15,694
less fancy than
everyone else's?

288
00:12:17,696 --> 00:12:20,448
Do you not trust me
with a fancy plate?

289
00:12:20,490 --> 00:12:23,493
No, honey, that's
a special plate.

290
00:12:23,535 --> 00:12:25,078
See, it's a game.

291
00:12:25,119 --> 00:12:27,664
Whoever gets
that plate wins.

292
00:12:27,706 --> 00:12:30,542
I can't believe I won.

293
00:12:32,043 --> 00:12:34,462
This is such a slap in the face.

294
00:12:34,504 --> 00:12:36,214
I mean, I'm your sister

295
00:12:36,256 --> 00:12:40,385
and you would give your baby
to these strangers over me.

296
00:12:40,427 --> 00:12:43,137
Monica is
Ross's sister.

297
00:12:43,179 --> 00:12:48,602
No, Ross's sister
was really fat.

298
00:12:48,643 --> 00:12:50,395
That was me.

299
00:12:50,437 --> 00:12:53,022
No, she was this really
dorky girl in high school

300
00:12:53,064 --> 00:12:55,609
used to follow Rachel around
like a puppy dog.

301
00:12:55,650 --> 00:12:58,194
Amy! You've got
to stop doing that.

302
00:13:03,908 --> 00:13:05,744
Okay, uh, listen,
I know that you're having

303
00:13:05,784 --> 00:13:07,161
a little bit
of a family crisis

304
00:13:07,203 --> 00:13:09,205
but you don't have
to take it out on the plates.

305
00:13:09,247 --> 00:13:12,584
In fact, I think
that everyone

306
00:13:12,626 --> 00:13:16,254
should cut their
food like this.

307
00:13:18,923 --> 00:13:20,007
Now, see?

308
00:13:20,049 --> 00:13:22,218
This way, you protect the plates

309
00:13:22,260 --> 00:13:24,429
and, let's face it,
you have fun.

310
00:13:25,972 --> 00:13:27,223
Okay, how
about this?

311
00:13:27,265 --> 00:13:28,725
If you guys die

312
00:13:28,767 --> 00:13:31,894
and the crazy
plate lady dies...

313
00:13:33,730 --> 00:13:35,607
then do I get the baby?

314
00:13:35,649 --> 00:13:37,233
No, if crazy plate la...

315
00:13:39,527 --> 00:13:41,488
If Monica dies

316
00:13:41,529 --> 00:13:43,782
then I would get Emma, right?

317
00:13:46,951 --> 00:13:48,328
Well, actually...

318
00:13:48,369 --> 00:13:50,037
Actually what?

319
00:13:50,079 --> 00:13:52,540
Uh... It's just
that in that case

320
00:13:52,582 --> 00:13:55,710
then, um... Emma
would go to my parents.

321
00:13:55,752 --> 00:13:57,003
What?

322
00:13:57,044 --> 00:13:58,338
Hurts, doesn't it?

323
00:14:00,965 --> 00:14:02,091
Uh...

324
00:14:02,133 --> 00:14:03,802
Who has to die
for me to get her?

325
00:14:11,351 --> 00:14:12,686
So, if Monica's
not around

326
00:14:12,727 --> 00:14:14,395
I'm not good enough
to raise Emma?

327
00:14:14,437 --> 00:14:17,023
No, that, that is
not what we're saying.

328
00:14:17,064 --> 00:14:18,024
Yeah, he's lying.

329
00:14:18,065 --> 00:14:19,066
He looked down.

330
00:14:20,568 --> 00:14:22,403
Well, what is
wrong with me?

331
00:14:22,445 --> 00:14:23,613
Am I incompetent?

332
00:14:23,655 --> 00:14:25,114
Because I managed to survive

333
00:14:25,156 --> 00:14:27,492
whatever it is
that killed the three of you.

334
00:14:29,035 --> 00:14:31,538
You're taking this
the wrong way.

335
00:14:31,579 --> 00:14:35,333
We think you are going
to be a wonderful parent.

336
00:14:35,375 --> 00:14:39,295
It's just, you're
more the, you know "fun" parent.

337
00:14:39,337 --> 00:14:41,881
Yeah, and we'd
want to make sure

338
00:14:41,922 --> 00:14:46,720
Emma has someone like Monica,
who's more of a disciplinarian

339
00:14:46,761 --> 00:14:48,596
someone who can be
firm and strict.

340
00:14:48,638 --> 00:14:50,473
That's not how
you see me, is it?

341
00:14:52,225 --> 00:14:54,018
No, you're
all about the fun.

342
00:15:00,941 --> 00:15:02,777
Look, I may not know
a lot about babies

343
00:15:02,819 --> 00:15:04,738
but do you really think
I'm not capable?

344
00:15:04,779 --> 00:15:07,031
No, you both are
equally capable.

345
00:15:07,073 --> 00:15:10,410
It's just, you're strongest
when you're together.

346
00:15:10,451 --> 00:15:12,245
Okay, so if
we both had Emma

347
00:15:12,286 --> 00:15:13,454
and I died...

348
00:15:13,496 --> 00:15:14,997
( knocks on table )

349
00:15:15,039 --> 00:15:16,875
she'd have to give her up.

350
00:15:16,915 --> 00:15:20,127
Sure. Monica would have
to give her up.

351
00:15:20,169 --> 00:15:22,463
I lie better than that, right?

352
00:15:24,841 --> 00:15:26,384
So let me get
this straight.

353
00:15:26,426 --> 00:15:28,636
So my two friends die,
I get Emma.

354
00:15:28,678 --> 00:15:30,638
Then my wife dies,
then Emma--

355
00:15:30,680 --> 00:15:33,474
the one tiny ray
of hope left in my life--

356
00:15:33,516 --> 00:15:34,768
gets taken away from me?

357
00:15:34,809 --> 00:15:36,935
There's your movie.

358
00:15:40,314 --> 00:15:42,066
Hey.

359
00:15:42,108 --> 00:15:43,234
There you are.

360
00:15:43,276 --> 00:15:44,944
You disappeared
after dinner.

361
00:15:44,985 --> 00:15:46,654
Oh, did somebody
miss me?

362
00:15:46,696 --> 00:15:49,783
Is there a child
to raise poorly?

363
00:15:49,824 --> 00:15:51,325
Ross and Rachel
don't know what

364
00:15:51,367 --> 00:15:52,702
they're talking about.

365
00:15:52,744 --> 00:15:55,204
I mean, it's not like
they're so responsible.

366
00:15:55,246 --> 00:15:57,624
Emma is the product
of a bottle of merlot

367
00:15:57,665 --> 00:15:59,333
and a five-year-old condom.

368
00:16:00,835 --> 00:16:02,169
Yeah, but they're right.

369
00:16:02,211 --> 00:16:03,922
I'm not a strong
father figure

370
00:16:03,963 --> 00:16:05,131
and I never will be.

371
00:16:05,172 --> 00:16:06,800
No, you learn
these things.

372
00:16:06,841 --> 00:16:08,008
You grow into it.

373
00:16:08,050 --> 00:16:10,177
Yeah, but it's not
who I am, you know.

374
00:16:10,219 --> 00:16:13,097
Everything they said
is exactly why I was worried

375
00:16:13,139 --> 00:16:15,141
about having a kid--
and it's true

376
00:16:15,182 --> 00:16:16,976
and, look, everybody knows it.

377
00:16:17,017 --> 00:16:17,977
I don't know it.

378
00:16:18,018 --> 00:16:19,813
I want to have
a kid with you

379
00:16:19,854 --> 00:16:21,439
because I think
you're going

380
00:16:21,481 --> 00:16:22,816
to be an amazing dad

381
00:16:22,857 --> 00:16:24,983
at the fun parts and
at the hard parts.

382
00:16:25,025 --> 00:16:26,945
Oh, yeah, well,
can you picture me saying

383
00:16:26,986 --> 00:16:28,655
"Go to your room--
you're grounded."

384
00:16:28,696 --> 00:16:31,324
Can you hear me say,
"You're grounded"?

385
00:16:31,365 --> 00:16:34,034
You said that
to me last week.

386
00:16:36,203 --> 00:16:37,413
How hard is it?

387
00:16:37,455 --> 00:16:39,874
No shoes on
the furniture!

388
00:16:44,629 --> 00:16:45,755
( groans )

389
00:16:45,797 --> 00:16:47,006
The producer from Days

390
00:16:47,047 --> 00:16:48,591
left a message
on my machine

391
00:16:48,633 --> 00:16:50,510
asking why I wasn't
at the parade.

392
00:16:50,551 --> 00:16:52,428
They said everybody's
pissed off at me

393
00:16:52,470 --> 00:16:54,889
and they all got to meet Santa.

394
00:16:54,931 --> 00:16:58,977
It's okay. I thought
of the perfect lie for you.

395
00:16:59,017 --> 00:17:00,269
It's easy to remember

396
00:17:00,311 --> 00:17:02,689
and it doesn't invite
a lot of questions.

397
00:17:02,730 --> 00:17:04,357
You weren't at the parade

398
00:17:04,398 --> 00:17:06,693
because you had
a family emergency.

399
00:17:06,734 --> 00:17:08,402
Oh, I like that, yeah.

400
00:17:08,444 --> 00:17:12,532
Wasn't at the parade because
I had a family emergency.

401
00:17:12,573 --> 00:17:13,741
Ooh, what happened?

402
00:17:13,783 --> 00:17:16,202
Uh... my sister's raccoon...

403
00:17:16,243 --> 00:17:17,912
Nothing with a raccoon!

404
00:17:17,954 --> 00:17:20,039
All right,
I'll take care of it.

405
00:17:20,080 --> 00:17:22,124
Oh, wait, what are you doing?

406
00:17:22,166 --> 00:17:23,459
Setting the table.

407
00:17:23,501 --> 00:17:25,127
Yeah, we thought
it might be nice

408
00:17:25,169 --> 00:17:27,881
to use the fancy china
for dessert, too.

409
00:17:27,922 --> 00:17:28,882
Oh, how nice.

410
00:17:28,923 --> 00:17:30,090
Maybe later we can all

411
00:17:30,132 --> 00:17:31,759
go blow our noses
on my wedding dress.

412
00:17:38,516 --> 00:17:39,809
Hey, dude, you okay?

413
00:17:39,851 --> 00:17:41,060
Sorry about before.

414
00:17:41,101 --> 00:17:42,395
Oh, no, that's okay.

415
00:17:42,436 --> 00:17:43,813
You're totally right.

416
00:17:43,855 --> 00:17:46,566
I don't know anything
about disciplining a child

417
00:17:46,607 --> 00:17:48,192
but it did hurt
my feelings

418
00:17:48,234 --> 00:17:50,403
and I want you to know
that if I die

419
00:17:50,444 --> 00:17:51,612
you don't get Joey.

420
00:17:59,119 --> 00:18:00,287
Uchh.

421
00:18:02,540 --> 00:18:03,666
Uchh.

422
00:18:06,377 --> 00:18:07,503
In case you
hadn't noticed

423
00:18:07,545 --> 00:18:08,588
I'm not talking to you.

424
00:18:08,629 --> 00:18:11,549
Uchh.

425
00:18:11,591 --> 00:18:14,510
You know, this is,
this is classic Rachel.

426
00:18:14,552 --> 00:18:15,720
Oh, yeah, yeah, right.

427
00:18:15,762 --> 00:18:17,137
Remember in high school

428
00:18:17,179 --> 00:18:19,223
when I died
and didn't give you my baby?

429
00:18:21,475 --> 00:18:24,645
This might be my one chance
to have a child, Rachel.

430
00:18:24,687 --> 00:18:26,647
I mean, you know
that I have been so busy

431
00:18:26,689 --> 00:18:27,857
focusing on my career...

432
00:18:27,899 --> 00:18:28,983
What?!

433
00:18:29,025 --> 00:18:30,109
What career?!

434
00:18:30,150 --> 00:18:32,194
Um... I'm a decorator.

435
00:18:32,236 --> 00:18:35,782
You decorate Dad's office
and now you're a decorator?

436
00:18:35,823 --> 00:18:38,743
Okay, I went
to the zoo yesterday.

437
00:18:38,785 --> 00:18:40,661
Now I'm a koala bear.

438
00:18:43,121 --> 00:18:45,374
Why can't you ever
be supportive?

439
00:18:45,416 --> 00:18:47,167
Sup... You want
to talk supportive?

440
00:18:47,209 --> 00:18:48,878
You didn't even
come and visit me

441
00:18:48,920 --> 00:18:51,213
when I was in the hospital
having the baby.

442
00:18:51,255 --> 00:18:53,841
Oh, yeah, well, you didn't
come to see me in the hospital

443
00:18:53,883 --> 00:18:55,384
when I was getting my lips done.

444
00:18:55,426 --> 00:18:57,011
Oh!

445
00:18:57,053 --> 00:18:59,013
I did the first time.

446
00:18:59,055 --> 00:19:00,222
Oh. Oh.

447
00:19:00,264 --> 00:19:02,182
And you know what?

448
00:19:02,224 --> 00:19:04,518
You want to know why
I am not giving Emily to you?

449
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:05,519
Emma.

450
00:19:05,561 --> 00:19:07,313
Whose side are you on?

451
00:19:08,314 --> 00:19:09,523
I'm not giving you Emma

452
00:19:09,565 --> 00:19:11,567
because there is no way
you could handle

453
00:19:11,609 --> 00:19:13,152
the responsibility of a child.

454
00:19:13,193 --> 00:19:14,654
Well, how hard could it be?

455
00:19:14,695 --> 00:19:15,655
You do it.

456
00:19:15,696 --> 00:19:17,698
Ooh-hoo-hoo-hoo.

457
00:19:20,743 --> 00:19:22,036
Do you want to know why

458
00:19:22,078 --> 00:19:23,788
you don't want me
to have the baby?

459
00:19:23,830 --> 00:19:25,164
Uh-huh.

460
00:19:25,205 --> 00:19:27,125
Because you don't
want me to be happy.

461
00:19:27,166 --> 00:19:29,627
You have always
been jealous of me.

462
00:19:29,669 --> 00:19:30,962
Jealous of what?

463
00:19:31,004 --> 00:19:33,464
Of your lack
of responsibility?

464
00:19:33,506 --> 00:19:35,341
Your, your immaturity?

465
00:19:35,382 --> 00:19:38,011
Your total disregard
for other people's feelings?

466
00:19:38,052 --> 00:19:39,386
Uh, to name a few.

467
00:19:41,848 --> 00:19:43,099
You know

468
00:19:43,141 --> 00:19:45,101
you just, you've
always been like this.

469
00:19:45,143 --> 00:19:48,187
You had to have everything
and I couldn't have anything.

470
00:19:48,228 --> 00:19:51,024
Like in junior high,
when you stole Timmy from me.

471
00:19:51,065 --> 00:19:54,027
I mean, do you even realize
how much that hurt me?

472
00:19:54,068 --> 00:19:56,696
Timmy was my boyfriend
and you made out with him!

473
00:19:56,737 --> 00:19:58,865
Oh, come on, that
was 20 years ago. Get over it.

474
00:19:58,906 --> 00:20:00,324
Oh. I cannot believe it!

475
00:20:00,366 --> 00:20:02,785
I cannot believe
that I invited you here today!

476
00:20:02,827 --> 00:20:05,163
Yeah, well, you know
what I cannot believe?

477
00:20:05,204 --> 00:20:07,040
That my so-called sister

478
00:20:07,081 --> 00:20:09,876
gets a 30% discount
from Ralph Lauren

479
00:20:09,917 --> 00:20:12,378
and I still have to pay retail?

480
00:20:12,419 --> 00:20:14,714
Ha-ha-ha. A-ha-ha.

481
00:20:14,755 --> 00:20:16,382
It's for 45.

482
00:20:17,383 --> 00:20:19,552
You bitch.

483
00:20:21,554 --> 00:20:24,057
You just think
you're so perfect

484
00:20:24,098 --> 00:20:25,599
with your new baby

485
00:20:25,641 --> 00:20:27,935
and your, your small apartment.

486
00:20:28,936 --> 00:20:30,897
Well, let me tell
you something.

487
00:20:30,938 --> 00:20:34,608
Your baby isn't even that cute.

488
00:20:35,609 --> 00:20:37,570
Too far, Amy.

489
00:20:37,611 --> 00:20:38,738
Too far.

490
00:20:41,574 --> 00:20:43,034
You take that back.

491
00:20:43,076 --> 00:20:43,910
No.

492
00:20:43,951 --> 00:20:45,203
Take it back.
No!

493
00:20:45,244 --> 00:20:46,537
What are you
going to do, make me?

494
00:20:46,579 --> 00:20:48,581
Hey, man, I work out.

495
00:20:50,624 --> 00:20:52,085
So do I.

496
00:20:52,126 --> 00:20:53,127
I do Pilates.

497
00:20:53,169 --> 00:20:54,170
I do yoga.

498
00:20:54,212 --> 00:20:55,337
Bring it on!

499
00:20:55,379 --> 00:20:56,630
Put the plates
back in the boxes!

500
00:20:56,672 --> 00:20:58,507
Put the plates back
in the boxes!

501
00:21:00,093 --> 00:21:01,969
Did you just push me?

502
00:21:02,011 --> 00:21:03,345
Uh, yeah. I think I did.

503
00:21:03,387 --> 00:21:04,847
All right, that's it.

504
00:21:04,889 --> 00:21:06,974
Okay, forget the bubble
wrap! There isn't time!

505
00:21:09,643 --> 00:21:11,979
Frizzy, frizzy,
frizzy, frizzy!

506
00:21:16,525 --> 00:21:18,485
Oh, my God!
Shouldn't we stop this?!

507
00:21:18,527 --> 00:21:20,154
What are you, out
of your mind?

508
00:21:20,196 --> 00:21:21,989
Let's throw some
Jell-O on them.

509
00:21:23,199 --> 00:21:25,034
( spitting )

510
00:21:25,076 --> 00:21:27,369
Ew! Gross!

511
00:21:39,757 --> 00:21:41,467
All right, that is it!

512
00:21:41,508 --> 00:21:43,136
This is our apartment

513
00:21:43,177 --> 00:21:44,804
and you cannot
behave this way.

514
00:21:44,845 --> 00:21:46,180
Now, if you can't
act your age

515
00:21:46,222 --> 00:21:47,807
then you shouldn't
be here at all.

516
00:21:47,848 --> 00:21:49,600
Now, those plates
may not be as nice

517
00:21:49,642 --> 00:21:51,894
as the pretty pink ones
that I picked out...

518
00:21:53,604 --> 00:21:55,273
but they're very
important to Monica

519
00:21:55,355 --> 00:21:56,649
and I want you to apologize

520
00:21:56,690 --> 00:21:58,818
to her right now.

521
00:21:58,859 --> 00:22:00,611
I'm sorry.

522
00:22:00,653 --> 00:22:01,612
Mon, I'm so sorry.

523
00:22:01,654 --> 00:22:03,156
Okay. That's better.

524
00:22:03,197 --> 00:22:06,159
Now, I want you
to apologize to each other

525
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:07,243
and mean it.

526
00:22:07,285 --> 00:22:09,245
Sorry.
Sorry.

527
00:22:09,287 --> 00:22:11,622
By the way, that fight
was totally arousing.

528
00:22:16,627 --> 00:22:18,963
Dude. Well done.

529
00:22:19,005 --> 00:22:20,214
You know what?

530
00:22:20,256 --> 00:22:22,341
If I die, and Rachel
dies and Monica dies

531
00:22:22,382 --> 00:22:24,177
you can totally
take care of Emma.

532
00:22:24,218 --> 00:22:26,679
Oh, yeah? Well, thanks.

533
00:22:26,720 --> 00:22:30,390
So, so... now
do I get Joey?

534
00:22:31,725 --> 00:22:33,102
Okay, but
you should know

535
00:22:33,144 --> 00:22:34,478
he eats
five times a day

536
00:22:34,520 --> 00:22:36,272
and shoves pennies
up his nose.

537
00:22:41,319 --> 00:22:43,237
Are you okay, Mon?

538
00:22:43,279 --> 00:22:44,446
Uh-huh.

539
00:22:44,488 --> 00:22:45,781
I mean, these
things happen.

540
00:22:45,823 --> 00:22:47,783
I mean, it's just a plate.

541
00:22:47,825 --> 00:22:49,869
It's not like
somebody died.

542
00:22:49,910 --> 00:22:52,163
It's all right,
you can mourn.

543
00:22:52,205 --> 00:22:54,999
Thank you,
it was so beautiful.

544
00:22:58,336 --> 00:23:00,880
I'm going to go to Joey's
and get the pies.

545
00:23:00,921 --> 00:23:03,090
Actually, not pies.

546
00:23:03,132 --> 00:23:04,842
It's just pie.

547
00:23:05,843 --> 00:23:08,137
I don't care.

548
00:23:08,179 --> 00:23:11,182
Oh, my God, I've lost
the will to scold.

549
00:23:15,853 --> 00:23:17,063
Look, Amy.

550
00:23:18,856 --> 00:23:20,107
I got a little, uh...

551
00:23:20,149 --> 00:23:22,276
a little out
of control over there.

552
00:23:22,318 --> 00:23:23,903
Um...

553
00:23:23,944 --> 00:23:25,238
And I'm sorry.

554
00:23:25,279 --> 00:23:29,033
You're my sister,
and if it really means

555
00:23:29,075 --> 00:23:30,910
that much to you...

556
00:23:30,951 --> 00:23:33,162
So you're going to
give me the baby?

557
00:23:33,204 --> 00:23:35,413
No, I was going
to let you use

558
00:23:35,455 --> 00:23:37,415
my Ralph Lauren discount.

559
00:23:38,542 --> 00:23:40,753
You are not going
to regret this.

560
00:23:43,130 --> 00:23:44,382
( baby crying )

561
00:23:44,422 --> 00:23:46,300
Oh, she needs changing.

562
00:23:46,342 --> 00:23:47,801
Oh, no, no, no.
I'll get her.

563
00:23:47,843 --> 00:23:50,137
I am super-competent,
totally responsible

564
00:23:50,179 --> 00:23:52,014
and fourth in line
to raise Emma.

565
00:23:52,056 --> 00:23:53,557
I'll be right there, Emma.

566
00:23:53,599 --> 00:23:56,018
Just let me get my trusty
diaper bag here.

567
00:24:02,482 --> 00:24:03,692
Well, what do you know?

568
00:24:03,734 --> 00:24:05,778
I guess I'll be the one
who dies first.

569
00:24:15,537 --> 00:24:16,872
Hey, does Monica know

570
00:24:16,914 --> 00:24:18,665
about her broken
plates yet?

571
00:24:18,707 --> 00:24:19,499
No.

572
00:24:19,541 --> 00:24:20,293
Broke them all, huh?

573
00:24:20,334 --> 00:24:21,085
Yup.

574
00:24:21,127 --> 00:24:22,002
You going to tell her?

575
00:24:22,044 --> 00:24:23,129
Nope.

576
00:24:24,546 --> 00:24:25,881
Hey.

577
00:24:25,923 --> 00:24:27,674
So I'm going to put
the plates back.

578
00:24:27,716 --> 00:24:29,343
You know,
I think you were right.

579
00:24:29,385 --> 00:24:30,636
I don't think we should

580
00:24:30,677 --> 00:24:32,512
use these plates again
for a long time.

581
00:24:32,554 --> 00:24:34,056
Like only if
the queen comes?

582
00:24:34,098 --> 00:24:36,267
Maybe not even then.

583
00:24:37,643 --> 00:24:38,811
Hey, I did it.

584
00:24:38,852 --> 00:24:40,146
I called my producer.

585
00:24:40,187 --> 00:24:41,314
I told him I had
a family emergency.

586
00:24:41,355 --> 00:24:42,689
He totally bought it.

587
00:24:42,731 --> 00:24:44,150
Thanks for teaching me
how to lie, Pheebs.

588
00:24:44,191 --> 00:24:45,151
No problem.

589
00:24:45,192 --> 00:24:46,402
Next week, stealing.

590
00:24:48,028 --> 00:24:48,988
'Bye, plates.

591
00:24:49,029 --> 00:24:50,156
Oh, you told her

592
00:24:50,197 --> 00:24:51,740
you broke all the plates, huh?

593
00:24:53,909 --> 00:24:54,994
What?!

594
00:24:55,035 --> 00:24:56,912
Something happened
with the plates?

595
00:24:56,954 --> 00:24:59,457
Uh... yeah, this, uh...

596
00:24:59,497 --> 00:25:01,499
raccoon came in...

597
00:25:01,541 --> 00:25:05,587
